>  I think (and someone will probably verify this from source) that polymorph-
>ing creatures only alters the mode of attack, and probably hit points. I
>once polymorphed a shopkeeper into a xorn; when the xorn killed me, it took my
>possessions! This would indicate that it was still attacking as a shopkeeper?
>Does anyone have similar experiences? What about polymorphing the dog into
>something more useful? Does it still attack as a dog?
I have successfully utilised a wand of polymorph to do some fun things.  My
dog has been a fog cloud, a Gnome, a long worm, and a demon before.  I liked
it best when he was a demon- made for a really nasty pet.  And it still ate
tripe rations.  When I turned a shopkeeper into a quivering blob, he still
got angry, but when I killed him I had an ordinary corpse...  With all the
gold, of course, hee hee.  Didn't lose any powers, either, I don't think.
